Usually, if one doesn't get far in the game, there's no single item that
would make it possible to let him _advance to a higher stage_; one would
need a lot of items and still wouldn't learn what's the really important
tactics (and strategies) to play. It's partly illusion and often just
plain hope that let people focus so much on wishes.

> Then, I've ascended. I've gone through Hell both with and without a 
> magic  lamp and I consider that keeping the magic lamp for Hell is 
> better than an  early wish.

Mind, that a guaranteed light source is much more crucial in the unlit
mines than in Gehennom; in Gehennom it's primarily just convenience, but
in the mines it will increase you survival rate significantly. (Of course
any lamp will do, but be sure that you light will last until mind end and
back up again.)

